  "body": "https://websockets.spec.whatwg.org/#dom-websocket-websocket says\r\n\r\n> Let *client* be [this](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#this)'s [relevant settings object](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#relevant-settings-object).\r\n\r\n*client*  is used for base URL for parsing relative URLs. This was introduced in https://github.com/whatwg/websockets/pull/45\r\n\r\nI think \"relevant\" should be \"current\". See https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/39978#issuecomment-1548543999\r\n\r\n> WebSocket spec says to use the relevant settings object, but going by the example in https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#realms-settings-objects-global-objects there's no way to test for the relevant settings object for a constructor (vs a method), since you can't use `.call()` with a constructor.\r\n>\r\n> I used `current` instead, like [Workers](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/workers.html#dom-worker), but this needs a spec change. ",
